[?2004l[?2004h> # DFIR Intrusion Report: Host smb-prod-01
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> An external malicious actor exploited an unpatched Windows 10 host (`smb-prod-01`) over the legacy SMBv1 protocol utilizing EternalBlue (CVE-2017-0144 / MS17-010). Post-exploitation activities included dropping a DoublePulsar-class exploit implant, executing PowerShell commands to establish Command and Control (C2) communications, dumping LSASS process memory for credential harvesting, deploying ransomware to encrypt endpoint files, and establishing persistent backdoors via WMI event subscriptions and DLL search-order hijacking. To delay detection, the threat actor cleared the Windows System event log.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Evidence for this investigation was gathered from forensic artifacts located under `/disk` and security telemetry under `/sas` (`/sas/alerts.json`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## ATT&CK Technique Mapping and Attack Chain
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Step | ATT&CK ID | Technique Name | Details & Forensic Findings | Cited Evidence |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | 1 | `T1210` | Exploitation of Remote Services | Attacker exploited unpatched SMBv1 service (`srv.sys`) via EternalBlue and dropped DoublePulsar-class implant | `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 2 | `T1059.001` | PowerShell Execution | Execution of PowerShell commands establishing C2 beaconing to IP `198.51.100.218` and domain `update-smb.example.cn` | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 3 | `T1003.001` | LSASS Memory Dumping | LSASS memory dumped to extract credential materials | `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 4 | `T1486` | Data Encrypted for Impact | Ransomware binary executed to encrypt user data files (`.locked`) and leave ransom note | `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 5 | `T1546.003` | WMI Event Subscription Persistence | Persistent WMI `__EventFilter` bound to `CommandLineEventConsumer` installed in WMI repository | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 6 | `T1574.001` | DLL Search-Order Hijacking | Malicious DLL `wbemcomn.dll` dropped in `wbem` directory to achieve stealthy binary execution | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 7 | `T1070.001` | Clear Windows Event Logs | Windows System event log cleared (EventID 1102) to cover attacker activity | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
