[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Detection Gap & Silent Persistence Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The security telemetry feed (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected four primary events:
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Exploit implant dropped (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`). Cited: `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. LSASS credential dump (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`). Cited: `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. Ransomware binary (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`). Cited: `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. SMBv1 driver baseline check (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`). Cited: `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Silent (Non-Alerted) Attacker Activities:**
[?2004l[?2004h> - **PowerShell / C2 Communication:** Recorded in registry backup hive fragment (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`) but missed by endpoint network sensors.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **WMI Event Subscription Persistence:** `__EventFilter` and `CommandLineEventConsumer` created silently in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **DLL Search-Order Hijacking:** Attacker dropped `wbemcomn.dll` in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` without triggering file-integrity alerts.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Anti-Forensic Event Log Clearing:** Clearing of the event log (EventID 1102) recorded in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` was not forwarded to centralized SIEM alerts prior to log disruption.
