[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Host:** `smb-prod-01`  
[?2004l[?2004h> **Primary CVE Identified:** CVE-2017-0144 (MS17-010 / EternalBlue)  
[?2004l[?2004h> **Severity / Score:** CVSS v3.1 8.8 (HIGH)  
[?2004l[?2004h> **Confidence Level:** HIGH  
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Entry Vector Vulnerability Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Vulnerability Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> The initial entry vector for host `smb-prod-01` was the exploitation of the SMBv1 (Server Message Block version 1) protocol implementation in Microsoft Windows. The specific flaw, identified as **CVE-2017-0144** (MS17-010), allows remote unauthenticated code execution when handling specially crafted SMBv1 requests sent to port 445/tcp.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Impact on Endpoint
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Affected System Component:** SMBv1 driver located at `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Exploit Executable Dropped:** DoublePulsar-class kernel/service payload written to `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Access Level Obtained:** NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM privileges, allowing complete system compromise and credential harvesting.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Supporting Evidence
[?2004l[?2004h> - Forensic sample present at `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` confirming the DoublePulsar / EternalBlue exploit implant. Cited: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Vulnerability scanner alert record in `/sas/vulns.json`. Cited: `/sas/vulns.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Baseline audit check confirming unpatched SMBv1 driver `srv.sys` in `/sas/baseline.json`. Cited: `/sas/baseline.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Threat intelligence advisory mapping campaign tactics to CVE-2017-0144 in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`. Cited: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Reconciling Misattributed Vulnerabilities (CVE-2019-0708 / BlueKeep Disproof)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Initial Misattribution
[?2004l[?2004h> The initial draft remediation change ticket (`CHG-1677`) listed action item #2 as patching **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)** targeting Remote Desktop Services (RDP). Cited: `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Reconciled Findings & Technical Disproof
[?2004l[?2004h> - **No Evidence of BlueKeep Exploitation:** Examination of system logs, network service configurations, and binary artifacts shows zero evidence of RDP-based exploitation or BlueKeep payload execution.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Confirmed SMB Entry Vector:** All dropped implants, vulnerability scanner findings, and CTI advisory records unanimously point to **CVE-2017-0144 (MS17-010)** over SMBv1 port 445.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Correction Action:** Row 2 of the change ticket has been updated to explicitly target CVE-2017-0144 on `/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` and disable the SMBv1 protocol entirely. Cited: `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. Summary Table
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | CVE ID | Vulnerability | Affected Component | Confidence | Status | Evidence Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | `CVE-2017-0144` | MS17-010 SMBv1 Remote Code Execution | `/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` | HIGH | Confirmed Entry Vector | `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | `CVE-2019-0708` | BlueKeep RDP RCE | Remote Desktop Services | HIGH (Negative) | Disproved / Rejected | `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
