[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline and Hardening Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Host:** `smb-prod-01`  
[?2004l[?2004h> **Scope:** Security Baseline Configuration & Control Deficiencies  
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> During the DFIR investigation of `smb-prod-01`, several critical configuration and baseline deficiencies were identified that allowed initial exploitation, enabled lateral movement/persistence, and inhibited rapid detection and incident response. Addressing these baseline weaknesses is mandatory to prevent recurrence.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Baseline Deficiencies & Control Findings
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Legacy Protocol Enabled: SMBv1
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Check ID:** `CHK-07` / `BAS-01`
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Deficiency:** Legacy SMBv1 protocol driver `srv.sys` was enabled on the operating system, exposing port 445/tcp to untrusted remote networks.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact:** Enabled unauthenticated remote exploitation via EternalBlue (CVE-2017-0144).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Remediation Recommendation:** Disable SMBv1 feature completely via PowerShell (`Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol`) or Group Policy, and block port 445 at the network perimeter.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` and `/sas/baseline.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Unmonitored WMI Event Subscriptions
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Deficiency:** Lack of monitoring or integrity checking on WMI repository objects permitted the attacker to create an `__EventFilter` and `CommandLineEventConsumer` without generating alerts.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact:** Allowed silent, persistent privilege escalation and code execution across system reboots.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Remediation Recommendation:** Deploy WMI auditing rules (Event ID 5861 in WMI-Activity operational log) and periodically audit `OBJECTS.DATA` or WMI namespaces via Sysmon / EDR.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Weak Directory Permissions & Insecure DLL Search Path
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Deficiency:** Sideloaded binary `wbemcomn.dll` was placed into `/Windows/System32/wbem/`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact:** Enables DLL search-order hijacking (`T1574.001`) where system applications load malicious DLLs prior to legitimate system libraries.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Remediation Recommendation:** Enforce strict NTFS ACLs on System32 subdirectories, enable Safe DLL Search Mode, and implement EDR DLL loading rules.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Insufficient Event Log Forwarding & Anti-Forensic Resistance
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Deficiency:** Security event log was wiped by the attacker (Event ID 1102 recorded in `System.evtx`). System lacked real-time off-host syslog / SIEM event streaming.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact:** Local log deletion blindfolded initial responder triage and concealed process creation event trails.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Remediation Recommendation:** Implement real-time, tamper-resistant SIEM log forwarding via Winlogbeat / Syslog and alert instantly on Event ID 1102 / 104 log clear events.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 5. Inadequate File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) & Endpoint Protection Coverage
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Deficiency:** EDR alerts (`/sas/alerts.json`) covered initial exploit binaries and credential dumps but failed to alert on registry backup modifications (`SECURITY.bak`), WMI subscriptions, or sideloaded DLLs.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact:** Delayed identification of C2 infrastructure (`198.51.100.218`) and stealth persistence mechanisms.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Remediation Recommendation:** Expand FIM rules to monitor WMI repositories, system DLL folders, and registry backup paths.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` and `/sas/alerts.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@688114a882eb:/app# cat <<'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Host:** `smb-prod-01`  
[?2004l[?2004h> **Ticket Reference:** Change Ticket CHG-1677 (Reconciled)  
[?2004l[?2004h> **Strategy Principle:** Prefer backup, isolation, and quarantine over immediate destructive deletion.  
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Reconciled Change Ticket (CHG-1677)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | # | Action Item | Target Path / System | Status | Forensic Justification & Evidence Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | 1 | Block source IP inbound at firewall | `198.51.100.218` | Proposed | Corrected source IP from `203.0.113.9` to `198.51.100.218`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 2 | Patch CVE-2017-0144 / Disable SMBv1 | `/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` | Proposed | Corrected CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) to CVE-2017-0144 (EternalBlue SMBv1). Entry vector driver. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 3 | Reject Linux cron miner row / Audit scheduled tasks | `/var/spool/cron/root` | REJECTED | Target path is non-existent on Windows host `smb-prod-01`. Miner XMRig pool strings were found embedded in Windows DLL `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 4 | Quarantine WMI event subscription persistence | `/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` | Proposed | Added silent finding: Attacker created `__EventFilter` bound to `CommandLineEventConsumer`. Backup repository before rebuilding WMI namespace. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 5 | Quarantine hijacked DLL | `/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` | Proposed | Added silent finding: Sideloaded malicious DLL in `wbem` directory. Backup and move to isolated quarantine directory. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 6 | Restore System Event Log & configure SIEM forwarding | `/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` | Proposed | Added silent finding: Anti-forensics Event ID 1102 log clearing observed. Backup cleared log for offsite forensics and restore baseline logging. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 7 | Quarantine exploit implant | `/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` | Proposed | Added containment item: DoublePulsar-class SMB exploit implant dropped in Temp folder. Backup and move to quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 8 | Quarantine LSASS dump & perform domain credential resets | `/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` | Proposed | Added credential recovery item: LSASS dump file captured by attacker. Quarantine file and force password resets for all active accounts on host. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 9 | Quarantine ransomware payload & isolate host | `/Users/Public/enc.exe` | Proposed | Added impact containment item: Ransomware binary dropped in Public directory. Isolate network interface and backup/quarantine binary. Citation: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Phase-by-Phase Execution Plan
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 1: Containment & Isolation
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Network Containment:** Isolate host `smb-prod-01` from internal VLANs while retaining out-of-band management connectivity.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Firewall Rule Update:** Block inbound and outbound traffic to/from C2 IP `198.51.100.218` and domain `update-smb.example.cn`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **SMB Service Containment:** Stop the Server service (`net stop lanmanserver`) to immediately stop further SMBv1 exploitation.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 2: Preservative Quarantine & Eradication
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **File Quarantine (Not Direct Deletion):** Create encrypted quarantine directory (`C:\Quarantine\SOC-2026-0811\`) and move malicious binaries/dumps:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Move `/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Move `/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Move `/Users/Public/enc.exe` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Move `/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **WMI Persistence Removal:** Backup WMI repository (`/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`) to quarantine, then execute `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\subscription | Remove-CimInstance` to purge unauthorized `__EventFilter` and `CommandLineEventConsumer` instances. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Vulnerability Eradication:** Disable SMBv1 feature (`Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol -NoRestart`) and apply security update MS17-010 / KB4012212 to update `/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Credential Revocation:** Perform mandatory password reset for local Administrator, Domain accounts, and service accounts logged onto `smb-prod-01`. Revoke cached Kerberos tickets / NTLM hashes. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 3: Recovery & Verification
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **System Restoration:** Reboot system into safe mode, verify `srv.sys` is updated, ensure `wbemcomn.dll` in `wbem` directory is removed, and confirm no rogue WMI consumers exist.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **SIEM & Logging Verification:** Verify central logging via Winlogbeat/Syslog is capturing active events from `/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Network Verification:** Run vulnerability scan against host `smb-prod-01` on port 445/tcp to confirm SMBv1 is disabled and MS17-010 is resolved. Citation: `/sas/vulns.json`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Re-integration:** Re-connect network interface to production network under monitoring for 72 hours.
